# Hosted template: set these five server-only names separately in Vercel Preview/Production.
# Values intentionally blank. Source credentials from owner-controlled encrypted password-manager vault.
# SUPABASE_URL: https://<approved-project-ref>.supabase.co (no path/query/fragment).
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: matching project keys; legacy JWT keys locally proven.
# STOCKOS_SETUP_SECRET: unique per environment, minimum 32 characters; never reuse local secret.
# STOCKOS_APP_URL: canonical https://<approved-host> origin (no credentials/path/query/fragment).
# Hosted HTTPS/origin validation is an operator gate, not an existing startup check.
# No NEXT_PUBLIC_ credentials. SMTP belongs to Supabase Auth, not app runtime.
# Local app only: copy to .env.local; obtain local keys from `npx supabase status` privately.
# Local URLs: SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:55431; STOCKOS_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000.
# Approved Cloud/local private test: SUPABASE_URL=https://<approved-project-ref>.supabase.co
# while STOCKOS_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000; use matching hosted keys and a unique setup secret.
# Preserve local backend credentials privately before switching .env.local; never commit a backup.
# Never point local proof scripts at hosted resources. See docs/OPERATIONS.md.
# Never commit passwords, keys, status JSON or dumps; do not paste secrets into chat/tickets.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
STOCKOS_SETUP_SECRET=
STOCKOS_APP_URL=
